  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solarization of WASH Infrastructure in Lebano</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cholera is a bacterial infection caused by a bacteria called Vibrio Cholera and can be caught by drinking or eating contaminated water and food. The first case in the region was detected in Syria on the 10th of September 2022. The virus rapidly spread, crossing the border into Lebanon. The first cholera case in Lebanon was reported on the 5th of October, and by the 13th of October, Lebanon has reported 29 confirmed cases in Akkar and Baalbek governorates. Based on the current context of water service operation, there is a need to provide water pumping and chlorination stations, as well as other water infrastructure, with an alternative source of energy.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Level concentrating on Cholera hotspots</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Similar projects conducted by LRC WASH team for solarization of water pumping and chlorination station in North Lebanon reached 10,000 beneficiaries. Consequently, this project is expected to solarize 1 system and thus reach around 1,000 beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solarization of WASH Infrastructure in Lebanon, in response to both the Cholera outbreak and the economic / financial crisis</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aim is to Reduce the national risk of cholera transmission by ensuring an improved access to safe water within the host communities and the Syrian refugees in Informal settlements.</narrative>
  </description>
